Modifications
-------------

The vector source carries changes made by this project rather than by the
original author, which LGPL-3.0 requires be stated. Both were made on
2026-08-02 and neither redraws any card. Each file states its own on its face,
in a comment at the top.

Applying to both files:

  * The cards were moved apart onto a regular grid with a gutter between them.
    As drawn, cards abutted and shared a single hairline rule along each
    boundary, which the atlas cutter had to locate by ink coverage and tell
    apart from the court cards' inner frames. Only the position of each card
    changed; the artwork within each card is untouched.

Applying to `playing_card_assets_corner_pips.svg` alone:

  * Each ace and court card gained a suit pip in the blank margin at its top
    right. A fanned tableau column leaves only the top 45 of a card's 307 design
    units showing, and the deck places its corner suit pip below that line on
    every rank. Cards 2-10 stay legible there because their body pips reach up
    into the strip, but an ace has only a centre pip and a court has portrait
    frame, so a covered one could not be told from its same-coloured twin. The
    added pip repeats that card's own corner index pip at its own size, in a
    layer of its own; it covers no artwork, and no original element was edited.

So `playing_card_assets_large.svg` is the artwork as its author drew it, laid
out differently. Both changes are reproducible from the upstream file, and the
file before them is in this repository's history.

